MID_SE_Led_Buc_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_001: Hey, Buccar—you've been to Dagsion before,\nhaven't you?
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_002: I spent seven years in the imperial capital. But that\nwas more than 20 years ago.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_003: Come on, out with it. I want to hear stories from\nBuccar's wild youth.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_004: You started thinking about the good ol' days the\nminute we stepped through the Gate of the Gods.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_005: I was thinking about the good ol' days, eh? I might\nhave been.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_006: Dagsion is...where I first met your father.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_007: My father? I...I didn't know that.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_008: As I'm sure you're aware, Lord Guillermo was once\na praetor in the imperial capital.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_009: One day I saw your father conducting an inspection,\nso I stopped him and challenged him to a duel.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_010: A duel? Really? I can't imagine you turning your\nblade against my father.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_011: I was an immature lad and overconfident in\nmy abilities.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_012: After mastering the martial arts back in the county\nof Baphos, I came to the capital to find an employer.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_013: I thought measuring a person's strength was the best\nway to decide if they were worthy of serving.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_014: What a foolhardy hothead I was. Your father\ndefeated me and then some!
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_015: But I will never forget the hand he held out as I lay\nthere on the ground.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_016: Father never told me that story! But it sounds like\nboth of you were hotheads in your younger days.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_017: Lord Guillermo likely didn't think it was a story for\ninnocent young ears.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_018: But yes, when we were in the capital, his rise to\nfame was unparalleled.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_019: Lord Guillermo married Hilaria then soon after was\nmade viceroy of Cydonia...
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_020: And then you were born, milady, and he seemed\nhappier than I'd ever seen him.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_021: That's enough.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_022: I've got to go. I'm sorry I took up so much of\nyour time.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_023: Lady Leda...are you certain? Won't you please\nreconsider your quest for revenge.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_024: We can't go back in time, Buccar. And sentimentality\nis not a luxury I can afford.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_025: Even if I have to give up everything—everything—\nI will kill the one who took my father from me.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_C_026: Ahhh...
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_001: Buccar, were you able to get your hands on the\narrows we need?
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_002: Yes, milady. I negotiated with the supply unit and\nreplenished our stores.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_003: I see. Thank you. Ugh...
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_004: Milady? Have I...done something wrong?
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_005: How long do you plan to stay with me?
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_006: "How long"? What do you mean?
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_007: I've spent my life focused on killing Bertrand and on\ndestroying the people who framed Father.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_008: And that won't change. I won't stop chasing Bertrand\nuntil I get another chance to kill him...and succeed.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_009: But you... You've never had the chance to find your\nown happiness...
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_010: Milady, you're...worried about me?
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_011: You have changed. No. You've returned to how you\nonce were.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_012: Don't. Just give me an answer.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_013: The thing that keeps me going now is Lord\nGuillermo's dying wish.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_014: The day Cydonia fell, he gave me one final order:\n"Take care of Leilidahna."
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_015: I lost my lord that day, but you are alive and well.\nAnd that is the light I follow.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_016: Hm...
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_017: So, I will remain by your side until my life is over—\nno, until even my time in the underworld is over.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_018: I stood against you once, and you forgave me.\nAnd now I intend to serve you selflessly.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_019: What's more, we are at war, and I can be your shield.\nPlease, I beg of you, let me stay by your side.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_020: {SetColor=Gray}He lost so much and suffered so much. And still,\nhe never left me.{SetColor=Default}
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_021: I depend on you a great deal, Buccar. You will\ncontinue to accompany me...
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_022: and I will continue to seek my revenge. You will not\nleave me, do you understand?
MID_SE_Led_Buc_B_023: I understand, and I thank you.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_001: Fire magic! Lady Leda, get back! Urgh!
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_002: Buccar?! You bastard! Rrah!
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_003: Are you OK?! You...you shielded me!
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_004: Lady Leda, I'm relieved to see you're safe. You\nfought very well indeed.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_005: I see you've taken out all of our enemies. We should\nbe safe here, at least for now.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_006: Who cares! Are you hurt?! Please, please tell me it\nisn't serious!
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_007: Milady...what is the matter? It isn't like you to...\nto act so shaken.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_008: Seeing you like that in front of those flames...\nIt... It brought back memories of...of...
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_009: The Cydonia Massacre...
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_010: It's alright. As you can see, I'm fine.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_011: But you were ready to die, weren't you? That's why\nyou jumped in front of me with no hesitation.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_012: It's...as you say. I was reckless in my desperation to\nprotect you.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_013: I am sorry I caused you so much distress.\nI have failed you.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_014: No! You haven't! You've always been by my side...
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_015: You've always protected me!
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_016: Your praise...is more than I deserve.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_017: I've always wanted to tell you how sorry I am\nabout your burn scars.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_018: You protected me back then too. I've caused you so\nmuch pain.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_019: You have nothing to apologize for.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_020: I earned these scars protecting you. To me, they are\na medal of honor.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_021: You're such a fool! When the war's over, I'll give you\na real medal or some other reward. Just don't die!
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_022: Please, please promise me you won't die. I— I can't\nlose anyone else. Please, Buccar...
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_023: I promise. I will always be here for you.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_024: If you want to give me a reward, milady, make it a\nhandmade necklace...like you made as a child.
MID_SE_Led_Buc_A_025: Gods...you really are a fool...